p_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0914533646283199,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-1.3966393059440074e-05,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.31500358674949824,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.22567,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"SecureTech Innovations, Inc., a technology-driven company, develops and commercializes artificial intelligence-driven manufacturing systems, blockchain-based digital infrastructure, and automotive safety technologies in the United States. The company offers AI UltraProd, which specializes in AI-powered industrial 3D manufacturing technologies; and Piranha Blockchain, which develops Web3 security protocols, blockchain infrastructure, digital asset reserves and management systems, and cybersecurity solutions. It also provides Terra Nova Technologies (Top Kontrol product line), an anti-theft and anti-carjacking system that can safely stop a carjacking without any action by the driver. Additionally, it engages in the hardware sales of industrial 3D-printing systems and robots, recurring consumables and materials, printed-parts manufacturing contracts, service and support contracts, and sales of automotive anti-theft and anti-carjacking devices. The company was formerly known as Securetech, Inc. and changed its name to SecureTech Innovations, Inc. in December 2017. SecureTech Innovations, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is based in Roseville, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. J. Scott Sitra | President, CEO, Principal Executive Officer & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $134,676 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25 people. Revenue per employee of $309K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 228%/yr across its filed history. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Securetech Innovations, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $358M market cap on $8M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +448% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -214% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.0\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 0.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 12309% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":123.08828761351934},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Large open-market insider purchases (net $100.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Kao Lee Converts 170 Series A Preferred Shares into 1.7 Million Common Shares at Securetech Innovations","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/kao-lee-converts-170-series-a-preferred-shares-into-17-million-common-shares-at-securetech-innovations","date":"2026-10-26","timestamp":1793039631.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SecureTech\u2019s AI UltraProd Signs Letter of Intent for First U.S. 3D-Printed Residential Project in California","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/securetech-ai-ultraprod-signs-letter-133000058.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SecureTech Finalizes QStak Blockchain Joint Venture, Exclusive IP License, and Equity Investment","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/securetech-fin